// spec: MOD-014
//
// modules/BackRef imports this file back.  A cycle through the ROOT works the
// way a cycle between two ordinary modules does [MOD-012].
//
// ⚠️ The root used to be the one file never entered in the loader's map, so
// BackRef parsed it a SECOND time and the two copies did not share their names:
// the root's body printed, and then its own imported name was undefined.
//
// ⚠️ This is also the case that used to have no compiled form at all -- the
// duplicate made the emitter refuse with 'Two modules named ... is not supported
// by the C back end yet.'  Both processors run it now, identically.

uses 'modules/BackRef';

WriteLn ('root body ran');

WriteLn (ModName ());
